.SH NAME
__hhs_change_dir - Change the current working directory to a specific Folder.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
usage: __hhs_change_dir [-L|-P] [dirname]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the current working directory to a specific Folder.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
$1 (Opt)
[-L|-P] whether to follow (-L) or not (-P) symbolic links.
.TP
$2 (Opt)
The directory to change. If not provided, default DIR is the value of the HOME variable.
.SH DETAILS
.nf

    Options:
      -L    : Follow symbolic links.
      -P    : Don't follow symbolic links.

  Notes:
    - dirname: The directory to change. If not provided, default is the user's home directory
.fi
